# ============================================================
# BUILD SETTINGS THAT ARE PUBLIC ON PURPOSE
# ------------------------------------------------------------
# Vite inlines every VITE_* variable into the bundle, so anything
# here ships in the page and is readable by anyone who views
# source. That is fine for the one value below and fine for
# nothing else: a real secret goes in .env.local, which is
# gitignored, or in the host's own environment settings.
#
# THE GOOGLE OAUTH CLIENT ID IS NOT A SECRET. It names the app
# to Google; what actually guards the account is the Authorised
# JavaScript origins list on the client itself, so a copy of this
# string is useless from any other domain. src/lib/drive.js says
# the same thing at more length.
#
# Client: "Filmmakers Studio - Drive (browser)" in Google Cloud
# project `filmstudio-495419`. Origins registered on it:
#   https://ak-filmmaker-studio.vercel.app
#   http://localhost:5173   (npm run dev)
#   http://localhost:4173   (npm run preview)
# A new origin needs adding there or the token request is refused
# by Google before it reaches Drive.
#
# Vercel builds from git, so committing this is what makes the
# deployed build Drive-capable. An environment variable set in the
# Vercel dashboard overrides it if you ever need a second client.
# ============================================================
VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=186547817753-9lm47ogdm4gqvuvje2h97qfda1pv4min.apps.googleusercontent.com
